[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'In this video, we\'ll guide firsttime users&nbsp; through the basic operations and settings of&nbsp;&nbsp; the Luna Ultra Standard Bundle and Creator&nbsp; Bundle, helping you get started quickly. Unboxing. Luna Ultra is available in two bundles,&nbsp;&nbsp; the standard bundle and the creator&nbsp; bundle. Inside the bundles, you\'ll find'

[00:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'activating and inserting your micro SD card.&nbsp;&nbsp; Rotate the screen clockwise to power on&nbsp; the camera. Scan the QR code displayed on&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the screen or tap via NFC to go directly to&nbsp; the download page and install the Insta 360&nbsp;&nbsp; app. Open the app. Tap search camera on&nbsp; the homepage and connect to your device. Then tap activate. Once activation is successful,&nbsp; the camera is ready for use. The camera includes&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '47 GB of built-in storage and supports up to 1&nbsp; TBTE of external storage. To insert a micro SD&nbsp;&nbsp; card, open the protective cover of the card slot&nbsp; on the right side of the main unit. Insert the&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'micro SD card in the direction shown and press&nbsp; it in with your fingernail until it clicks into&nbsp;&nbsp; place. You can later pull down the menu and swipe&nbsp; from left to right to change the storage location. Powering off. To power off the device in&nbsp; horizontal shooting mode, simply rotate&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the screen counterclockwise back to its original&nbsp; position. You can customize the screen rotation&nbsp;&nbsp; action in settings, screen rotation operation.&nbsp; In vertical mode or adaptive horizontal,&nbsp;&nbsp; rotating the screen will not power off the device.&nbsp; Instead, it will switch to vertical shooting mode.&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'To power off the device in this mode,&nbsp; press and hold the shutter button. How to use. Use the joystick to control lens&nbsp; direction. Push the joystick in three times&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'or press the left button on the rotating&nbsp; screen to quickly flip shooting angles. Push the joystick in to enable autotracking.&nbsp; The camera will track the main person in the&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'frame. If no person is detected, it will&nbsp; track a general subject in the center area&nbsp;&nbsp; of the frame. Push the joystick in again to&nbsp; cancel tracking. Push and hold the zoom button&nbsp;&nbsp; for continuous zoom from one times to 12 times&nbsp; zoom. Short push the button to quickly switch&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'between them. Swipe left from the right edge&nbsp; of the screen to enable beauty mode effects. Press the shutter button to start recording.&nbsp; During recording, the indicator light will flash&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'red. Press the shutter button again to stop&nbsp; recording. By default, the camera is set to&nbsp;&nbsp; landscape mode. To switch to vertical shooting,&nbsp; swipe down to open the shortcut menu and select&nbsp;&nbsp; auto orientation or vertical mode. Rotating the&nbsp; screen will automatically switch the camera to&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'vertical shooting. Detaching the remote screen.&nbsp; Press and hold the release buttons on both sides,&nbsp;&nbsp; then gently pull to detach the remote screen. It&nbsp; can be used to control the camera remotely or as&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a microphone for audio capture. To reattach the&nbsp; remote screen, press and hold the release buttons&nbsp;&nbsp; on both sides. Align the top part and gently press&nbsp; downward until it is securely attached. Playback.&nbsp;&nbsp; After shooting, swipe right from the left edge&nbsp; of the screen to review your most recent footage.&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Charging. The camera uses USBC charging.&nbsp; Please use the official charger included&nbsp;&nbsp; in the box. During charging, the indicator light&nbsp; will remain solid orange. We recommend charging&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the camera while it is powered off. Tap the&nbsp; icons at the top of the display screen to&nbsp;&nbsp; check the battery levels of both the gimbal&nbsp; and remote screen. Thanks for watching the&nbsp;&nbsp; Luna Ultra quick start guide. Stay tuned for&nbsp; more tutorials from us. See you next time.'
